# openccu-lite release identity (ROADMAP D-44, replacing D-37). Read by lite-version.mk.
# VERSION is openccu-lite's own semantic version - the release identity, the /VERSION LITE= line,
# the artefact names (openccu-lite-<product>-<version>.<ext>) and the tag (v<version>).
# 1.0.0 is the first release. A prerelease build of the next version carries its prerelease part
# here (1.0.1-beta, ...) and is passed as LITE_VERSION=<VERSION>.<N>, N from the project's build
# list (never reused); a release is built with LITE-VERSION's VERSION as it is. The dev series
# ended with 1.0.0-dev.45, the beta series with 1.0.0-beta.14, the rc series with 1.0.0-rc.3; the
# update check orders dev < alpha < beta < rc < the release (task 291).
# 1.1.0-dev is the dev track of the next minor version after 1.0.0: its builds are 1.1.0-dev.<N>
# from 0, published as pre-releases (D-122); stable systems stay on 1.0.0.
# 1.1.0-beta is the beta track of the same version, from 1.1.0-dev.6: built as 1.1.0-beta.<N> from 0, pre-releases too (1.1.0-beta.0 was a lab build).
# 1.1.0 is the release of 1.1.0-beta.1's content, built as LITE_VERSION=1.1.0 (no prerelease part).
# 1.2.0-dev is the dev track of the next minor version after 1.1.0: built as 1.2.0-dev.<N> from 0, pre-releases (D-122); stable systems stay on 1.1.0.
# 1.2.0-rc is the rc track of the same version, from 1.2.0-dev.0: built as 1.2.0-rc.<N> from 0, pre-releases too; the beta and dev channels are offered them, stable stays on 1.1.0.
# 1.2.0 is the release of 1.2.0-rc.0's content, built as LITE_VERSION=1.2.0 (no prerelease part).
# 1.2.1 is a patch release after 1.2.0, built as LITE_VERSION=1.2.1 (no prerelease track).
# 1.3.0-beta is the beta track of the next minor version after 1.2.1: built as 1.3.0-beta.<N> from 0, pre-releases (D-122); stable systems stay on 1.2.1.
# 2.0.0-beta is the beta track of the next major version: eQ-3's HMIPServer 1.5.1 (a new HMIPServer is always a major version), built as 2.0.0-beta.<N> from 0, pre-releases (D-122); 2.0.0-beta.0 is a lab build.
# 2.0.0-rc is the rc track of the same version, from 2.0.0-beta.12: built as 2.0.0-rc.<N> from 0, pre-releases too (D-122); stable systems stay on 1.2.
# BASE is the OpenCCU-Base release the image is built from (3.89.14; the fork's OpenCCU-Base pin
# carries it as OPENCCU_BASE_COMPAT_VERSION), and the first thing a bug report names. It is
# OpenCCU-Base's version, not an OpenCCU release with its build date: the buildroot fork left
# OpenCCU's releases behind and is not rebased on them any more (D-127, 2.0.0-rc.0). /VERSION's
# VERSION= line is BASE, as a CCU3's /VERSION carries the eQ-3 release (task 396;
# board/lite/version-file.sh), and hmipserver's getVersion answers it.
VERSION=2.0.0-rc
BASE=3.89.14
